# Approve config and fund TicketAutomator and ReferralStorage contracts
Two new contracts were deployed to extend protocols functionality and support upcoming marketing campaign:

1. ReferralStorage (0x14d3c35B72523898c4a61F3B7E2F1f42D1D96B03): contract enables referrals functionality by letting anyone to register as referrer and promote our website with special referral url for earning rebates share from referred user's ticket generation.
2. TicketAutomator (0xD1950a138328B52Da4fE73DbdB167a83f2c83DB9): contract generates tickets by looping ETH\<>INT swaps multiple times. It is upgraded contract version with added possibilities: 1 - to implement cross chain (bridged) ticket generation, 2 - supplement (loan) additional WETH to user to enable full utilization of spent ETH, 3 - possibility to work in tandem with referrals processing contracts.

**This Tally vote meant to setup initial config for these contract, grant necessary access roles and fund them with required assets from treasury.**



Explanation of actions for ReferralStorage contract:

* setTier() function is called 4 times to initiate referral tiers and token lock amounts;
* 5M INT tokens transfer to ReferralStorage for initial rewards funding. Additional dedicated Tally vote for long-term referral campaign approval will be held later;
* grantRole() function is called to give ReferralStorage contract right to store data on DataStore contract (DATA\_ADMIN role);

Actions for TicketAutomator contract:

* setConfig() function is called to initiate working params and point to companion ReferralStorage contract;
* 4 WETH tokens transfer to TicketAutomator for loan functionality to work properly;
* grantRole() functions is called to give TicketAutomator special new role REFERRAL\_ADMIN to be able use functionality of ReferralStorage;

# IFT staking campaign extension for another 50 weeks
The IFT staking rewards introduced at the beginning of the year proved to be a success. 80 Lucky Hand IFTs were minted since the start of the campaign, but only -12 were burnt. A further 44 custom IFTs were minted and only -18 were burned. As a reminder, more than half of the Lucky IFTs were burned before the staking was introduced, so it slowed down the IFT burning and INT dumping considerably. The initial staking campaign was mean to last 10 weeks and will end on 2025-03-12. This Tally vote is to extend the staking campaign at the same rate for another 50 weeks (~1 year). The longer period will signal to IFT holders the long term vision of the project and make IFT (INT) holding even more comfortable and desirable.

Upon a successful vote 25M INT tokens will be transferred from the treasury to the RewardManager contract and then, using multisig, the funds will be added as staking rewards at 500k INT weekly rate for another 50 epochs (weeks) starting from epoch 13 (2025-03-27).



\---



P.S. This proposal is intended to replace the [previous one with same topic](https://www.tally.xyz/gov/internet-token-dao/proposal/52055817529518645080251554928403984830341026926489627492308931545485832507779) because it was misconfigured and can't be executed onchain.&#x20;

&#x20;

# Add Liquidity to Maverick Protocol 
This proposal is to transfer 10 million INT and 1 ETH to the multisig wallet for the purpose of creating a new INT-USDC Liquidity Pool (LP) on Maverick Protocol.

Maverick Protocol is a relatively small multi-chain DEX, founded in 2021 and backed by the likes of Coinbase and Pantera Capital. They are currently running a "Token Integration Reward Program" to help increase TVL on their platform as well as boost social visibility to token projects.&#x20;
[https://www.mav.xyz/blog/Maverick-Protocol-Token-Integration-Reward-Program](https://www.mav.xyz/blog/Maverick-Protocol-Token-Integration-Reward-Program)

By participating in this rewards program and creating a new liquidity pool on Maverick, we will give INT holders the option to participate in yield farming opportunities via trading fees and potential incentive programs. In addition to this newfound utility for INT holders, integrating with new protocols will give INT more opportunities for cross-promotion and help increase visibility across the Base network.&#x20;

Though this new LP will not directly generate fees for the Lottery prize pool, I believe that will mostly be a non-issue as the vast majority of lottery tickets are bought via the INT website which uses the main UniswapV3 LP. In addition, as this new LP grows over time, it will create the potential for *indirect* prize pool accumulation, as well treasury income via pool-to-pool price arbitrage.

# Remove PickCallbackV2 processor
To make INT protocol fully decentralized from beginning some functionality was attached to every INT token transfer. PickCallback contracts was responsible for decentralized weekly lottery draws and IFTs distributions. Although this only needs to be done once a week, attempts are made to do this for each INT token transfer. This behavior has not been a problem so far as such "empty" attempts thru the week have been very gas "friendly" (cheap). After the introduction of V2, a new PickCalbackV2 contract was deployed which additionally calls calculations/transfers for airdrops during each INT token transfer. As these calculations are quite complex this already causes problems and makes each INT token transfer very expensive. As example can be this tx: [https://basescan.org/tx/0x1f29dc0c83e38bcdea9b1631a95432998ef7b1cfd2c9f9916a9d0b34d5bf83c1](https://basescan.org/tx/0x1f29dc0c83e38bcdea9b1631a95432998ef7b1cfd2c9f9916a9d0b34d5bf83c1)

Buying tickets (1 ticket) with just 7 loops yielded 494 log entries and 28M gas usage with $3.11 tx fee because 35 (7\*5) airdrop calculations/transfers were processed alongside. After PickCallbackV2 removal ~100 such loops should be possible and will significantly lower average ticket price for small buyers.&#x20;



**This Tally vote proposes to completely remove (disable) PickCallbackV2** from protocol's workflow. At the moment the contract performs three call to already permission-less functions to other contracts and these functions have always been unrestricted and callable by anyone:

* rewardDistributor.pick() - initiate weekly lottery draw;
* nftDistributor.distribute() - distribute IFTs after weekly lottery draw;
* boostManager.process() - process airdrop calculations and distributions for 5 IFTs in turn;

Instead we will setup automatic processing once a week of rewardDistributor.pick() and nftDistributor.distribute() functions using [Gelato Web3 App Automation](https://www.gelato.network/web3-functions "https://www.gelato.network/web3-functions")

For boostManager.process() substitution we will create airdrop claim/compound UI on website. But it always will be possible (and was before) to process it manually by anyone using BoostManager's process(uint256\[]) function, providing IFT ids to process.  [https://basescan.org/address/0xeeefe02e2028780adb63d63a7bad0ad0896a1713#writeContract](https://basescan.org/address/0xeeefe02e2028780adb63d63a7bad0ad0896a1713#writeContract)

On the other hand this processing is even not necessary to get full airdrop distributions, because all accumulated rewards for all unclaimed periods are always processes on IFT burn.



PickCallbackV2 contract to remove with this Tally vote is:

[https://basescan.org/address/0xb03f595a68dd405231b27d74435a5b3fb88ed8bb#code](https://basescan.org/address/0xb03f595a68dd405231b27d74435a5b3fb88ed8bb#code)

# Approve RewardManager and fund initial airdrop campaign
A new contract [RewardManager ](https://basescan.org/address/0x19b30c4f5b86c3ec1334c0f96ce09f4071e2146f "RewardManager")(RM) has been deployed to make reward distributions, airdrop updates and working with external partners more flexible. Only several rewards management functions will be delegated to operational multisig wallet without handing over to it the crucial protocol configuration role or giving full access to treasury funds. After the successful vote multisig using this intermediate RM contract will be able to:

\- Seed Progressive Jack pot with tokens from RM;

\- Enable/Disable additional tokens for Progressive Jackpot (we will have tokens to win from partners later);

\- Add/Update INT and WETH staking rewards for IFTs using RM balance;

\- Stake/Unstake IFTs for contributor airdrop rewards bucket;

\- Send ETH or any token from RM back to treasury;

\- DAO itself can anytime recover ETH or any token from RM to treasury with Tally vote.

To properly setup this workflow CONFIG\_ADMIN role will be given to RM contract and new REWARD\_ADMIN role will be given to multisig for using restricted RM contract's functions. At the same time RewardDistributor config will be changed, to divert wethRewardSplit (10%) part of weekly lottery pot to RM.

Additionally with this vote 5M INT and 1 WETH will be transferred to RM contract to let multisig setup initial test IFTs airdrop campaign for 10 weeks (500k INT + 0.1 WETH weekly rewards).

The multisig address on base is [0x0c02d2d320c62d4088840a459fe8862c802fba78](https://basescan.org/address/0x0c02d2d320c62d4088840a459fe8862c802fba78 "0x0c02d2d320c62d4088840a459fe8862c802fba78")

It is a 4/7 multisig. Governance post on multisig establishment:

[https://gov.theinternettoken.com/t/operations-multisig/48](https://gov.theinternettoken.com/t/operations-multisig/48)

You can view the multisig holdings and transactions via the [Safe website](https://app.safe.global/home?safe=base:0x0C02d2D320C62d4088840a459fE8862C802fbA78 "Safe Website").

